.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.jsonl

# Runtime-generated by hooks — do not commit
hooks/governance-log.jsonl
hooks/aggregates/

# _test_fixtures/ holds two different kinds of thing, and the blanket
# "hooks/_test_fixtures/" rule that used to sit here called both runtime
# scratch. It never removed anything: three fixtures were already tracked and
# gitignore does not apply to tracked paths, so the rule's only real effect
# was to block NEW fixtures from ever being added. That is how
# unicode-hygiene-check.py came to ship with no way to run its test.
#
# Captured transcripts stay out: regenerable, and they carry live session
# content. The unicode-hygiene fixtures are the opposite, hand-authored test
# data where each file exists to pin one exact codepoint, so regenerating them
# is neither possible nor meaningful.
#
# The parent is globbed rather than named because git cannot re-include a path
# whose parent directory is itself excluded.
hooks/_test_fixtures/*
!hooks/_test_fixtures/unicode-hygiene/

# Runtime registry copy from test resolution — never publish vault inventory
.claude/
